  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1037 PM CDT Tue Jun 30 2026\n\nThe upper high will slowly drift eastward and begin to weaken as we \nprogress into the weekend. This will start a slow downward trend in \ntemperatures and upward trend in storm chances. The \"cooling\" will \nbe gradual, so we will not suddenly get rid of the dangerous \nheat. Heat indices will continue to be 100+ Friday through \nSunday. As we get into next week, weak troughing will slowly \ndevelop over Mississippi River Valley allowing our temperatures \nto settle back to near normal. \n\nIn regards to the Independence Day festivities, there will be some \nscattered showers and storms to dodge. The good news is that \ncoverage should decrease after sunset. Rain chances will begin to \nincrease on Sunday as the high loses the influence over the area.\nThose chances will increase further early next week as our \npattern becomes a bit more troughy and the low level moisture \nremains rich. As far as strong storm potential, a couple wet \nmicrobursts will be possible through the weekend with the water- \nloaded updrafts. In addition, rain rates will be high along with \nslow storm motion. This will pose a low localized flash flood \nthreat.",
